Negative: declaration of Skip[T comparable](v, skip T) T. The declared result type is the type parameter T, which
does not implement error, so the Target is rejected with "has no error result" (exit 2), although the only instance,
Skip[error], returns error and call sites of it are accepted (skip_comparable_call). This follows the documented
error-result predicate (the declared result type is error or implements it); recorded as a limit, not as a bug.
